            <ArticleTitle>Mechanisms of myocardial ischemia in a patient with left main coronary artery atresia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>764-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes the different clinical and instrumental manifestations of coronary ischemia in a patient with left main coronary artery atresia. Exercise test and thallium-201 perfusion scintigraphy during isometric exercise test were negative for angina and electrocardiographic changes. Conversely, dipyridamole infusion caused severe angina, marked ST-segment changes and diffuse thallium-201 uptake abnormalities. This peculiar anatomical condition offers the opportunity of high-lighting the role played by the microcirculation in determining myocardial ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
